# paper-trading-bot environment config
#
# This bot's default setup (scan, replay:raw, replay:memory) needs NO
# environment variables at all — market data comes from Coinbase's public
# Exchange candles endpoint, which requires no API key and has no
# order-placing capability.

# Optional. When set, the periodic reflection step (every 10 new closed
# trades) asks Claude to reason over the actual recent trades and propose a
# bounded settings change, instead of the deterministic two-lever heuristic
# in src/reflect.ts. Every proposed value is clamped in code before it's
# ever applied — see src/llmReflect.ts. Leave unset to use the heuristic
# only; nothing else about the bot changes either way, and it never places
# any order regardless.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The variables below are placeholders for an OPTIONAL future paper-trading
# broker/exchange adapter. Do not set these unless you have verified,
# paper/test-mode-only credentials for that specific venue — and even then,
# never commit a real .env file (it is already in .gitignore).

# Example only — uncomment and fill in if you wire up a verified paper broker:
# BROKER_VENUE=alpaca
# BROKER_API_KEY=
# BROKER_API_SECRET=
# BROKER_PAPER_MODE=true
# LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=false
